# One CI gate, one file. Issue #991 moved the gate list out of
# `.github/workflows/release.yml`, the repository's third most conflicted path,
# because its step list was append-only. A gate lives here instead, so two
# branches adding gates create two files, never one shared region.
# `rust-script scripts/run-ci-gates.rs --stage <stage>` runs them.
ci_gate check_js_rust_translation
  stage web
  description "R1000: the committed js -> rust translation (rust/tests/fixtures/js-rust-translation/, data/meta/js-rust-translation.lino) is for the current bytes of every module in scope, its totals are the sums of its rows, and the layered-ci js-rust job checks meta-language out at the ledger's commit. Seconds, no upstream checkout; the js-rust job re-translates, compiles and runs the calls."
  run "node scripts/translate-js-rust.mjs --verify"
  justification "A js->rust translation that drifts from its source module causes the Rust tier to run stale logic without a compile error; the gate was introduced in PR #1188 R1000 (commit 7a8d109fe) to keep the translation byte-current."
